        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Arshile Gorky, Eve Beglarian, Alice Mason\n- Roles: painter, composer, performer, audio producer, abstract artist\n- Places: Ann Arbor, Michigan, New York\n- Concepts: Abstract Expressionism, Armenian descent\n\nFacts:\n- Arshile Gorky was born as Vostanik Manoug Adoian on April 15, 1904, and he became an Armenian-American painter.\n- Alice Mason had settled in New York by 1927.\n- Alice Mason was influenced by the early abstract artist Arshile Gorky.\n- Arshile Gorky had a seminal influence on Abstract Expressionism.\n- Arshile Gorky died on July 21, 1948.\n- Eve Beglarian was born in Ann Arbor, Michigan, on July 22, 1958.\n- Eve Beglarian is a contemporary American composer, performer, and audio producer of Armenian descent.",
